<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - see Disposition__c.field-meta.xml
        in this folder for why a comment above the root breaks `sf` deploy.

        Twin of Outgoing_Broker__c in this same folder; read that file's comment for the full
        role-named-lookup, lookupFilter and relationship-name-collision reasoning. relationshipName
        Incoming_Broker_Changes is distinct from Outgoing_Broker__c's Outgoing_Broker_Changes and
        free on the Contact parent (measured against the same five existing Contact lookups).

        Same SetNull seed hazard as Outgoing_Broker__c: scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex mass
        deleting broker Contacts SetNull's this lookup too. Incoming_Broker_Firm__c is the
        snapshot that survives it.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 RECONCILED 2026-08-20 (code review). SAME FIX AS Outgoing_Broker__c IN THIS FOLDER.
        =====================================================================================
        This field's <lookupFilter> was still testing Contact.Is_Broker__c = True despite the
        object's own comment already documenting the move to the Contact.Broker record type.
        Measured live on usman-dpeg the same day:
            SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Contact WHERE Is_Broker__c = true                 -> 0
            SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Contact WHERE RecordType.DeveloperName='Broker'   -> 19
        <filterItems> now reads Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName = 'Broker'. errorMessage and
        inlineHelpText below no longer name Is_Broker__c.
    -->
    <fullName>Incoming_Broker__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The broker Contact who replaced the outgoing one. Incoming_Broker_Firm__c stamps this Contact's firm at write time so the row still reads correctly if this Contact is later deleted.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>The broker who replaced the outgoing one. Only Contacts on the Broker record type appear.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Incoming Broker</label>
    <lookupFilter>
        <active>true</active>
        <booleanFilter>1</booleanFilter>
        <errorMessage>Only Broker Contacts can be selected here.</errorMessage>
        <filterItems>
            <field>Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Broker</value>
        </filterItems>
        <isOptional>false</isOptional>
    </lookupFilter>
    <referenceTo>Contact</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Incoming Broker Changes</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Incoming_Broker_Changes</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
